From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ben Bangert <ben@groovie.org>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] modprobe: keep dots in modalias names

filename2modname() stops copying at the first '.' to strip ".ko", and
modprobe runs both the requested name and every modules.alias wildcard
through it. A devicetree modalias with a versioned compatible, such as
of:NgpuT(null)Cqcom,adreno-635.0Cqcom,adreno, is cut at the dot and can
never match, so the Adreno GPU on the Dragon Q6A never autoloads msm.
Skip the truncation when the name contains a ':', as every modalias does.
---
--- a/modutils/modutils.c
+++ b/modutils/modutils.c
@@ -86,7 +86,7 @@
 char* FAST_FUNC filename2modname(const char *filename, char *modname)
 {
 	char local_modname[MODULE_NAME_LEN];
-	int i;
+	int i, alias;
 	const char *from;
 
 	if (filename == NULL)
@@ -98,7 +98,12 @@
 	// 'basenamization' was here in the first place.
 	//from = bb_get_last_path_component_nostrip(filename);
 	from = filename;
-	for (i = 0; i < (MODULE_NAME_LEN-1) && from[i] != '\0' && from[i] != '.'; i++)
+	/* Modaliases and alias wildcards always contain a ':', module names and
+	 * filenames never do. Devicetree compatibles such as qcom,adreno-635.0
+	 * carry a version dot; truncating there makes the kernel's modalias
+	 * unmatchable, so autoload silently fails. */
+	alias = (strchr(from, ':') != NULL);
+	for (i = 0; i < (MODULE_NAME_LEN-1) && from[i] != '\0' && (alias || from[i] != '.'); i++)
 		modname[i] = (from[i] == '-') ? '_' : from[i];
 	modname[i] = '\0';
 
